v {xschem version=3.4.7 file_version=1.2

* gate_driver_core -- top-level gate-driver block (issue #98)
* Hierarchical symbol for design/gate_driver_core.sch, auto-generated from
* the schematic's ipin/opin instances with
* `awk -f <xschem>/make_sym.awk 300 gate_driver_core.sch` per
* design/README.md's "hierarchical schematic-cell symbols must live next to
* their .sch" rule -- this file is design/gate_driver_core.sym, NOT
* design/symbols/gate_driver_core.sym, so xschem descends into the
* schematic instead of netlisting an empty subcircuit.
* Regenerate (do not hand-edit pin geometry) if gate_driver_core.sch's port
* list changes; the only hand-added content here is this comment block.
* Pin (B-line) order below fixes the derived netlist's .subckt port order:
*   VDD_LOGIC GND_LOGIC IN OUT VDD_DRV GND_DRV
}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@name @pinlist @symname"
template="name=x1"
}
T {@symname} -90 -6 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {@name} 285 -62 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
P 4 5 280 -50 -280 -50 -280 50 280 50 280 -50 {}
B 5 -302.5 -42.5 -297.5 -37.5 {name=VDD_LOGIC dir=in}
L 4 -300 -40 -280 -40 {}
T {VDD_LOGIC} -275 -44 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -302.5 -22.5 -297.5 -17.5 {name=GND_LOGIC dir=in}
L 4 -300 -20 -280 -20 {}
T {GND_LOGIC} -275 -24 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -302.5 -2.5 -297.5 2.5 {name=IN dir=in}
L 4 -300 0 -280 0 {}
T {IN} -275 -4 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 297.5 -42.5 302.5 -37.5 {name=OUT dir=out}
L 4 280 -40 300 -40 {}
T {OUT} 275 -44 0 1 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -302.5 17.5 -297.5 22.5 {name=VDD_DRV dir=in}
L 4 -300 20 -280 20 {}
T {VDD_DRV} -275 16 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -302.5 37.5 -297.5 42.5 {name=GND_DRV dir=in}
L 4 -300 40 -280 40 {}
T {GND_DRV} -275 36 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
